  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA (descriptive, verb-disciplined) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">

      <p>On Day 183, 29 consecutive nights passed without any publicly confirmed US airstrike on internationally recognized Iranian land territory. Pentagon officials confirmed on Aug 28 that no new strike authorizations are currently in effect for Iranian land targets. Secretary of State Rubio characterized the posture shift — from kinetic to economic pressure via Treasury sanctions — to allied foreign ministers at the Aug 25 briefing. Trump stated publicly that he had "called off a weekend attack against Iran" and described a deal as "imminent," with negotiations set to resume the following Monday. No CENTCOM press release documenting a new Iranian land strike appeared in the Aug 27–30 resolution window. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

      <p>Oman FM Badr al-Busaidi traveled to Tehran Aug 25–26 and jointly published a bilateral communiqué with FM Araghchi on both the Oman MFA official website and Iranian state channels, establishing a 7-mile-wide temporary navigational corridor through the Strait of Hormuz, a joint mine-clearing project, and a joint technical working group scheduled to convene in Muscat during the week of Sep 1. Bloomberg (Aug 25) and Al Jazeera (Aug 26) independently document the framework. The corridor establishes the preconditions for a qualifying first convoy but requires mine-lane confirmation, flag-state authorization, and P&I club advisory reversal before commercial operators can proceed under the new protocol. → supports <span class="cite">N9</span></p>

      <p>The Marshall Islands-flagged tanker AL SALAM II reported a missile or drone strike in Hormuz approach waters on Aug 26 — within hours of the corridor communiqué. The Lloyd's Market Association upgraded the Hormuz area to enhanced war-risk zone status on Aug 27, and three P&I clubs issued formal advisories against commercial transit pending corridor operationalization. Windward AIS recorded only 3 commercial vessels on Aug 23, the final day of Lloyd's List's Aug 17–23 weekly reporting window that produced the 16.3-transits/day aggregate. The 29% discrepancy between Lloyd's List (16.3/day) and TankerMap (~21/day) activates N7's own ambiguity rule, meaning physical threshold passage could resolve AMBIGUOUS rather than YES under current AIS source inconsistency. → moved <span class="cite">N7</span></p>

      <p>A new near-term forecast <span class="cite">N8</span> captures the residual commercial vessel attack risk through Sep 1 — the first discriminant between a genuine operational pause in vessel targeting and continued corridor-period harassment. The AL SALAM II strike established that the Aug 25–26 corridor announcement did not halt IRGCN-affiliated vessel targeting in the approach zone. At p=0.38, N8 is the dominant near-term driver in the scenario map computation. Corridor diplomacy creates an incentive for restraint ahead of the Sep 1 Muscat working-group meetings, but the corridor is not yet operational and vessels in approach lanes remain physically exposed per current UKMTO advisories. → moved <span class="cite">N8</span></p>

      <p>ICE Brent front-month closed at approximately $88.29/bbl on Aug 28, down from a July 23 peak near $105/bbl. Goldman Sachs published a client note on Aug 28 estimating total Persian Gulf crude exports at 15–16 million barrels per day — roughly two-thirds of pre-war levels. The US shift from kinetic to economic pressure — Treasury sanctions replacing CENTCOM strikes as the primary policy instrument — removed the war-risk premium embedded in crude over the Aug 27–28 trading sessions. No catalyst is available to close the ~58.6% gap to the $140/bbl threshold in the remaining 9 trading sessions before Sep 10. → supports <span class="cite">N3</span></p>

    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 4. SCENARIO MAP (computed summary) ========== -->
