      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path (15%):</strong> N8 YES (p=38%) triggers a cycle of retaliatory US pressure and IRGCN vessel attacks that collapses the corridor framework before the Sep 1 Muscat technical meetings can produce an operational protocol.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (53%):</strong> N8 NO, corridor framework holds as a diplomatic construct but N9 also fails — operational prerequisites (mine clearance, insurance, flag-state authorization) are not met within the 14-day window, and Hormuz transits remain below 15/day through late September while negotiations continue.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (32%):</strong> N8 NO, N9 YES — a confirmed first convoy completes transit under the corridor protocol before Sep 12, P&I clubs begin reversing advisories, and N7 probability rises substantially toward the 15-transits/day threshold before EOD Sep 21.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 5. INSIDE IRAN (descriptive, ~200 words) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · 200 words · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>

      <p>Iranian state channels — IRNA, Tasnim, and IRIB — broadcast the joint Iran-Oman communiqué on Aug 26 with the framing that the corridor framework was a product of Iranian diplomatic initiative, not concession to external pressure. Press TV English-language coverage emphasized FM Araghchi's role as equal co-author of the 7-mile-wide temporary protocol and presented the joint mine-clearing project as a mutual security arrangement rather than an Iranian compliance obligation. Iranian Port and Maritime Organization statements published on Tasnim characterized the corridor as consistent with full Iranian sovereignty over strait navigation management. → supports <span class="cite">N9</span></p>

      <p>No independently verified public in-person appearance by Mojtaba Khamenei was documented in the Aug 27–29 window via any open-source channel. Iranian state media's most recent public-facing material — a photograph and a sub-15-second video attributed to Aug 10 from Mehr News — remains unverified by any TIER1 international outlet. Misbar's Aug 23 fact-check explicitly labeled widely circulated Khamenei videos as 2022-era footage. President Pezeshkian's claim of a ~7-hour private meeting on Aug 10 comes exclusively from an Iranian government source and does not satisfy the N4 resolution criteria for independent verification. → supports <span class="cite">N4</span></p>

      <p>IRIB and Press TV presented the US shift from airstrikes to Treasury sanctions as confirmation that kinetic pressure had reached its practical limit. No Iranian state media reporting documented any resumption of IAEA monitoring access or any communication from the AEOI regarding enrichment downblending cooperation. All three prerequisites for N6 resolution — IAEA monitoring restoration, confirmed active downblending under supervision, and IAEA Director General completion report — remain absent from Iranian domestic reporting and from the Aug 29 IAEA public statements register. → supports <span class="cite">N6</span></p>

    </div>
  </div>

